// Ch4 C4-13 "Boss: the Spar-Wraith", the way in (docs/kb/story/beats/act1_ch04.md §5). The derelict's
// main deck under the mainmast, about 08:10, a low sun through the set sails. D05: the wraith in the
// rigging, tilted up through the sails against the sun, wrapped in its own sail-membrane like a shroud,
// its wounds bleeding held cyan. The lines move with no hand on them. The battle barks (§5, <= 35
// words) are spoken here, before the fight: the engine has no in-battle barks yet. Asha says nothing
// aloud to the wraith. Its motes are held and hang without sinking, and the sails stay set: both are the
// Canticle's payoff at the name board (M4-A2P-116 B2). Nothing lifts.
// The fight is on the derelict's deck, never the ferry's (ADR 0017 (d)). Four in the party: three
// active, one in reserve. Music: spar_wraith (stem 1). The chapter flow opens ch04_spar_wraith next.
title: ch04_spar_wraith
location: ch04/brightwater_ferry
---
@letterbox on
@camera D05
@vfx glimmer_held at=derelict_rigging count=8 rate=hang
@music spar_wraith fade=1.0
@wait 2.0
Ysolde [neutral]: Stand back from the rigging, please. #line:ch04_wraith_001
Toma [determined]: On my shield. #line:ch04_wraith_002
@letterbox off
===
